X86 grant-bump-vs-waiters-x86
(*
 * MV1 :first_target:, ON THE MODEL THAT DECIDES IT.
 *
 * STATUS: FIXED IN THE SOURCE -- `wakeAll` / `wakeOne` now fence before loading
 * `waiters`, and `grant-bump-vs-waiters-x86-FENCED.litmus` is what the shipped
 * code compiles to on this model. This file pins the UNFENCED shape and stays
 * required ALLOWED, because a Forbidden verdict with no Allowed control beside it
 * is free. It is NOT a regression barrier over `src/` -- a `.litmus` file is a
 * standalone model and no source change can move its verdict; that barrier is
 * `tests/check-fence-shape.sh` (`just test-fence-shape`), which disassembles the
 * shipped `wakeAll` / `wakeOne`. Everything below describes the code AS IT WAS.
 *
 * The C11 companion (`grant-bump-vs-waiters.litmus`) asks what the STANDARD
 * permits. This asks what x86-TSO permits, which is the question that was never
 * exercised because this code has only ever run on arm64.
 *
 * P0 is the publisher, `publishGrant` -> `wakeAll`:
 *     storeU32Release(value, cur + 1)   ->  a plain MOV store on x86
 *     loadU32SeqCst(waiters)            ->  a plain MOV load on x86
 * A release store needs no barrier on TSO and a seq-cst LOAD needs none either,
 * so the compiler emits two plain MOVs and NOTHING orders the store against the
 * later load.
 *
 * P1 is the waiter, `waitOn`:
 *     addU32SeqCst(waiters, 1)          ->  a LOCKed RMW: a full barrier
 *     loadU32SeqCst(value)              ->  a plain MOV load
 * The waiter's side is fully ordered by its own LOCK prefix. That does not help,
 * because the reordering that matters is P0's.
 *
 * The `exists` clause is the LOST WAKEUP: the publisher sees `waiters == 0` and
 * skips the wake syscall, while the waiter sees the OLD value and therefore parks
 * -- and the kernel's compare-and-park re-reads that same old value and puts it to
 * sleep.
 *
 * RESULT (herd7 7.58, 2026-08-17): **ALLOWED / "Sometimes 1 3"**. The window is
 * ARCHITECTURALLY REACHABLE on x86-TSO. See `-FENCED` for the remedy, and
 * ../README.md for what this does and does not license concluding.
 *)
{ value=0; waiters=0; 1:EBX=1; }
 P0                 | P1                 ;
 MOV [value],$1     | XCHG [waiters],EBX ;
 MOV EAX,[waiters]  | MOV EAX,[value]    ;
exists (0:EAX=0 /\ 1:EAX=0)
